id: pm-kcs4
title: Native pm context next and pm context focus with permanent navigation aliases
description: "The pm-n7rr target surface names 'context (next/focus)' as one noun. Today next and focus are separate top-level commands. Fold them as verbs of context (pm context next, pm context focus) while keeping pm next and pm focus working forever as hidden aliases — these are the highest-frequency agent commands, so migration hints must respect the ux.deprecation_hints suppression config from pm-0z7n. pm next actionability semantics (core/item/actionability.ts, PR#357) and pm focus session context (runtime/session.json, PR#257) are unchanged — grammar only. Duplicate check: pm-72xf (closed focus inheritance feature); no open overlap."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:cli",simplification
created_at: "2026-07-05T05:08:52.089Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:14.490Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:13.521Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-09T17:39:13.521Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "context noun exposes next and focus verbs with payloads identical to the standalone commands; pm next / pm focus keep working as aliases with suppressible hints; spelling-parity spec green; contracts, completions, docs, and MCP names regenerated; top-level help shows a single navigation noun."
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Delivered native context next/focus through shared SDK command contracts, permanent root aliases, coherent discovery and namespace-aware completion. Fish runtime schema flags now remain scoped to context snapshots."
expected_result: Native and compatibility navigation commands preserve SDK results and focus behavior; shell completion offers only flags belonging to the selected operation.
actual_result: Real temporary-workspace and npm/Bun acceptance passed; real Fish preserved context/ctx runtime fields and excluded them from focus/next; full suite and exact coverage passed.
