  "2026-09-09T04:24:15.265Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: native command node placement preserves existing SDK handlers; bootstrap aliases, runtime contracts, capability routing, package availability, positional addressing, and three shell completions share declared mappings. TDD reproduced missing namespace support, then verified native/legacy argv and real isolated tracker reads. Broader quality gates and package acceptance are in progress."
  "2026-09-09T04:42:05.181Z","harness:codex","Verification update: focused native/legacy and help/contract suite exercised 271 cases; 270 passed and one obsolete package-hint expectation was corrected. Native JSON help now retains optional-package installation recovery. GitHub live inventory found no open issues or PRs and no open Dependabot/code-scanning/secret-scanning alerts. Full coverage and static gates must finish before closure."
  "2026-09-09T04:56:37.103Z","harness:codex","Coverage checkpoint: all 8,637 tests passed; exact global coverage reported 99.99 statements, 99.98 branches, 99.98 functions, 99.99 lines. Added behavioral cases for the remaining eight branches, two functions and one line without exclusions or threshold changes; 26 focused tests now pass. Compact summary now suppresses duplicate root aliases only in unscoped summary mode, retaining full and explicit alias contracts; the unchanged completed-task token gate passes."
  "2026-09-09T05:15:20.146Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked sandbox-safe suite passed 42 tests across 8 files. Final typecheck passed across source, SDK type tests, packages, and examples. Compact contracts summary measured 4075 tokens versus the unchanged 4111-token ceiling; composite task measured 12631 versus 12667. Native context defaults and focus persistence passed real temporary-workspace and independent npm/Bun package acceptance."
  "2026-09-09T05:29:21.198Z","harness:codex","Final verification: 8639 tests in 655 files passed; exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (63818 statements, 48528 branches, 13248 functions, 61196 lines). Full static gates and source documentation requirements passed without relaxed thresholds. Linked suites, typecheck, secret scan, native/legacy temporary-workspace acceptance, real package installation, independent npm/Bun SDK consumers, and npx/bunx packed smoke with 13 packages passed. GitHub issue/PR and security alert inventories were clear before opening this delivery PR."
  "2026-09-09T16:51:27.523Z","harness:codex","Review verification: 8639 tests across 655 files passed, exact coverage 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (63823 statements, 48528 branches, 13252 functions, 61201 lines). Full static quality, typecheck and the 57-surface token gate passed without relaxed existing ceilings. Each canonical linked namespace suite passed 42 tests; the new token-measurement link passed 12 tests. CodeRabbit accepted the three strengthened test assertions. The latest pm-changelog 2026.9.9 is installed; outcome titles feed package-generated release notes. PR 1225 requires a fresh hosted review on the forthcoming push."
  "2026-09-09T17:17:23.079Z","harness:codex","Review round 2: reproduced the context runtime-field leak in real Fish completion (context focus offered --context-segment) and a failing focused assertion. The renderer now uses semantic context gating, preserving context/ctx snapshot flags while excluding focus/next. The focused suite passed 117 tests; real Fish passed three snapshot positives, five navigation negatives, and the native --clear flag. Full coverage and static verification are running."
  "2026-09-09T17:39:12.628Z","harness:codex","Final review correction verification: the isolated full suite passed 8639 tests in 655 files with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts: 63824 statements, 48530 branches, 13252 functions, 61202 lines. Full static quality and typecheck passed; both items passed both sandboxed linked commands. Real Fish reproduced the original leak and passed context/ctx positives plus focus/next negatives after correction. All touched named callables have descriptive JSDoc by AST inspection; this is scoped evidence, not a repository-wide function-documentation percentage. Every received review artifact was reacted to and replied to; the baseline-reset finding was rejected with unchanged-ceiling measurements. Final hosted verification follows the correction push in PR 1225."
